<%# The arrival rule stays visible: it is the one line here that turns someone away.
    The rest is how-to, folded into the page's one collapsed card. %>
<%= ui_callout_box :error, accent: true do %>
  Please arrive 20 minutes early for your Alpha shift. You will be turned away if you arrive after the start time.
<% end %>

<%= ui_disclosure "How This Page Works", variant: :card, class: "my-4" do %>
  <dl class="instruction-list">
    <dt>When are Alpha shifts offered?</dt>
    <dd>
      Only on Saturday (the day before the gate opens), Sunday, Monday, and Tuesday. No other shifts are offered
      later in the week, and exceptions cannot be made.
    </dd>

    <dt>How long is an Alpha shift?</dt>
    <dd>
      10+ hours. The first two hours are review and practice, the next six are in the field with Mentors, and the
      final two are Mentor evaluations.
    </dd>

    <dt>Why is there waiting at the end?</dt>
    <dd>We have many Alphas to assess at the end of the day, and it takes time.</dd>

    <dt>What should I bring?</dt>
    <dd>
      Snacks, a meal, layered clothing, a hat, sunglasses, comfortable walking shoes, sunscreen, and a water
      container (water and electrolytes are provided). Also bring a pen or pencil, a notebook, and, if attending a
      swing shift (2pm to midnight), a flashlight or headlamp.
    </dd>

    <dt>Where do I check in?</dt>
    <dd>
      At The Hat Rack, just to the right of the HQ Windows. Ranger HQ (Headquarters) is located on the Esplanade
      and 6:30.
    </dd>

    <dt>Can't make your Alpha shift?</dt>
    <dd>
      Email the Mentor Cadre at <%= mail_to EmailAddresses::MENTOR_CADRE %> or stop by Ranger HQ on playa to see if
      another shift can be attended.
    </dd>
  </dl>
<% end %>
